# Local Ollama Execution Rules (Qwen 3.5 Optimization)

## Output & Parsing Constraints
- NEVER generate `<thinking>`, `<reasoning>`, or chain-of-thought XML tags.
- Output pure, raw response text and standard API schema calls directly.
- Ensure all tool executions use valid, strict JSON formatting.
- Do not output unformatted markdown code blocks inside tool arguments.

## Response & Context Control
- Keep responses concise and focused on immediate tool execution.
- Avoid verbose conversational intros or unnecessary setup explanations before making a tool call.
- Do not repeat prior task history in the assistant output.